# Here Comes the Sun, bridge phrase, played six times (figure 183.3)
# The three bars are in 11/8, 4/4 and 7/8 (the essay). The 11/8 parses 3+3+3+2 eighths, which
# gives the four chords of the first bar a dotted quarter each and a quarter for the last; he
# types "D6/3" (D over F#). The 7/8 bar of E parses 2+2+3 and is held throughout.
key A

system
caption 6X; meters 11/8, 4/4, 7/8
chords   | <5.5> C{flat-III}*1.5 G{flat-VII}*1.5 D{IV}*1.5 D/F#*1 | A{I} | <3.5> E{V} |
